1
00:00:01,455 --> 00:00:04,910
Farewell, Blue Cop

2
00:00:06,512 --> 00:00:10,718
You can summon Mega Trucker any time you want with that card,

3
00:00:10,718 --> 00:00:11,955
and you can give him commands, too.

4
00:00:11,955 --> 00:00:13,954
Huh? What was that? What's going on out here?!

5
00:00:14,929 --> 00:00:17,059
- Huh???
- Uh, Uncle Edo...

6
00:00:22,564 --> 00:00:24,156
Stay away from Jun!

7
00:00:24,993 --> 00:00:26,346
W-wait!

8
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,757
Uncle Edo, were you in the repair shop?!

9
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:32,835
I dozed off while working late... then I was woken up by a loud noise outside!

10
00:00:34,835 --> 00:00:37,100
It was you! You were the one who broke my fence!

11
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,170
And ran over Jun's bike!

12
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:41,595
Aah, Uncle Edo, that's not what happened!

13
00:00:41,595 --> 00:00:42,673
It's a misunderstanding, I-

14
00:00:42,673 --> 00:00:44,578
Quiet, you! Don't come any closer!

15
00:00:52,899 --> 00:00:53,984
What are you doing?

16
00:00:53,984 --> 00:00:56,815
How dare you dodge that... you heap of scrap metal!

17
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:01,320
Please stop it. This is not safe!

18
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:02,554
What did you say?!

19
00:01:02,554 --> 00:01:06,747
Please stop! Blue Cop isn't a heap of scrap metal!

20
00:01:07,947 --> 00:01:09,210
He's from some planet called...

21
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:12,778
I am a Metal Cardbot. A mechanical lifeform from planet Machina.

22
00:01:12,778 --> 00:01:13,914
Right, that's the one!

23
00:01:13,914 --> 00:01:16,999
Why did you come to Earth? Are you trying to invade or something?!

24
00:01:16,999 --> 00:01:18,968
No no no, sir! We are...

25
00:01:20,325 --> 00:01:22,444
Hey, who are you calling, Edo?

26
00:01:22,444 --> 00:01:26,188
I'm calling the cops, why? Do you think the army should be handling this?

27
00:01:26,587 --> 00:01:27,756
T-that's not a good idea, sir!

28
00:01:27,756 --> 00:01:29,259
Please, stop him, Blue Cop!

29
00:01:29,457 --> 00:01:30,088
Right.

30
00:01:30,918 --> 00:01:32,709
Ah, hello? Is this the army headquarters-

31
00:01:33,109 --> 00:01:34,531
Waah!

32
00:01:35,303 --> 00:01:38,079
Let me go!

33
00:01:38,079 --> 00:01:41,456
You're just trying to threaten me to keep me quiet, aren't you?!

34
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:48,286
We have to clear up this misunderstanding somehow.

35
00:01:48,286 --> 00:01:49,621
What should I do?

36
00:01:49,621 --> 00:01:52,962
Just untie me already... my shoulders are killing me!

37
00:01:52,962 --> 00:01:55,513
Blue Cop. Do something about his shoulders.

38
00:01:55,513 --> 00:01:56,450
His shoulders?

39
00:01:56,450 --> 00:02:00,150
Yes! Show him you're not a bad robot after all.

40
00:02:13,485 --> 00:02:19,680
I heard on the radio that delivering a vibration of 3200 hertz helps blood circulation and relaxes the muscle.

41
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,984
Woah!

42
00:02:21,966 --> 00:02:26,288
Ohh... that's good... that's the spot. Try to really get in there...

43
00:02:33,401 --> 00:02:35,103
Ugh...

44
00:02:35,235 --> 00:02:36,400
Are you alright?

45
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:41,157
No, I'm not... I'm tired and thirsty. Could you get me some coffee?

46
00:02:42,324 --> 00:02:43,615
Yes, sir.

47
00:02:48,039 --> 00:02:49,918
So you really can make coffee!

48
00:02:49,918 --> 00:02:52,276
It's a basic skill for surviving on planet Earth.

49
00:02:52,276 --> 00:02:54,819
One sugar and no cream, okay?

50
00:02:54,819 --> 00:02:56,341
Yes, sir!

51
00:03:02,728 --> 00:03:03,931
Here you are.

52
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:13,160
Augh, why is it so sweet?!

53
00:03:14,889 --> 00:03:16,908
By one sugar, did you mean... one cube?

54
00:03:16,908 --> 00:03:19,875
Are you trying to give me diabetes?!

55
00:03:23,632 --> 00:03:25,811
Where are you going?

56
00:03:25,811 --> 00:03:29,810
To work. I have a business meeting this morning that I have to prepare for.

57
00:03:29,810 --> 00:03:34,312
And you! Make sure to get this mess cleaned up while I am gone!

58
00:03:37,348 --> 00:03:38,912
Hey, kid!

59
00:03:39,412 --> 00:03:41,877
You look like you need help. Want a hand?

60
00:03:41,877 --> 00:03:43,456
This voice is from...

61
00:03:43,456 --> 00:03:44,758
Mega Trucker?

62
00:03:45,258 --> 00:03:47,469
Jun! Let's summon Mega Trucker!

63
00:03:47,469 --> 00:03:49,932
Summon? You mean... bring him back out?

64
00:03:49,932 --> 00:03:54,478
Yes. A Metal Cardbot that has been sealed cannot act against their master. In this case, you.

65
00:03:54,478 --> 00:03:55,627
There's no need to worry.

66
00:03:59,264 --> 00:04:01,205
Alright, I'll give it a try.

67
00:04:01,608 --> 00:04:03,655
Metal Breath, pickup!

68
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,576
Mega Trucker, setup!

69
00:04:12,431 --> 00:04:15,693
I may not look it, but such delicate work is my specialty.

70
00:04:15,693 --> 00:04:17,471
Are you sure about that?

71
00:04:17,471 --> 00:04:20,322
Leave it to me. Music START!

72
00:04:30,374 --> 00:04:32,177
Mega Trucker, you're pretty good!

73
00:04:33,821 --> 00:04:35,237
I'm just getting started!

74
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:40,360
Woohoo!

75
00:04:43,891 --> 00:04:44,858
Stop it!

76
00:04:47,759 --> 00:04:50,432
Don't get in my way! This is my favorite part!

77
00:04:55,105 --> 00:04:56,850
Woohoo!

78
00:05:00,377 --> 00:05:04,588
Aah! Both of you, knock it off! Stop fighting and start getting along!

79
00:05:05,850 --> 00:05:07,750
...Did you guys finish clean-

80
00:05:12,372 --> 00:05:14,987
WHAT IS THIS?!

81
00:05:17,798 --> 00:05:19,855
What do you have to say for yourselves?

82
00:05:19,855 --> 00:05:21,901
W-We're very sorry.

83
00:05:22,821 --> 00:05:25,305
Oh, that's right! My meeting is starting soon.

84
00:05:25,305 --> 00:05:27,185
I can't waste any more time.

85
00:05:27,975 --> 00:05:30,605
And don't get into any more trouble while I'm gone!

86
00:05:34,182 --> 00:05:36,199
Jun, don't you have to go to school too?

87
00:05:36,199 --> 00:05:38,185
O-Oh, that's right!

88
00:05:41,509 --> 00:05:43,932
Why is nothing going my way today!?

89
00:05:45,896 --> 00:05:48,495
Looks like you need some help with that!

90
00:05:48,495 --> 00:05:51,665
Blue Cop! I have a job for you!

91
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:03,338
So you can transform into a car.

92
00:06:03,338 --> 00:06:04,555
Yes.

93
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:09,216
Wait...  so are all these cars friends of yours?

94
00:06:09,709 --> 00:06:10,358
Huh?

95
00:06:17,391 --> 00:06:18,951
There's a bad traffic jam.

96
00:06:18,951 --> 00:06:20,634
Augh, but I'm in a hurry!

97
00:06:20,634 --> 00:06:21,896
I'll do my best.

98
00:06:21,896 --> 00:06:24,350
Wait, what are you going to do?

99
00:06:29,687 --> 00:06:31,382
Woah, woah, woah! Watch out!

100
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:40,838
Oh!

101
00:06:43,485 --> 00:06:44,809
Hang on, stop the car!

102
00:06:44,809 --> 00:06:46,498
Come on, I said stop!

103
00:06:54,514 --> 00:06:57,461
Police sirens should only be used in serious situations!

104
00:06:57,461 --> 00:06:59,516
This wasn't one! And besides,

105
00:06:59,516 --> 00:07:02,103
You aren't even a real police car!

106
00:07:02,103 --> 00:07:03,526
...I'm sorry, sir.

107
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:09,126
Hmm... I have something important to discuss.

108
00:07:16,636 --> 00:07:18,504
Uncle Edo! I'm back!

109
00:07:18,504 --> 00:07:20,826
Oh, Jun! What's up?

110
00:07:20,826 --> 00:07:22,947
Were you able to make it to the meeting?

111
00:07:22,947 --> 00:07:25,038
Uhh... yeah.

112
00:07:25,439 --> 00:07:26,542
What about Blue Cop?

113
00:07:26,542 --> 00:07:29,230
You should just forget about that robot.

114
00:07:29,230 --> 00:07:30,689
What do you mean?

115
00:07:33,625 --> 00:07:37,235
I promise not to tell anyone about you. But in return, you gotta leave.

116
00:07:37,235 --> 00:07:41,370
I can't do that! As you know, Jun has the Metal Breath, sir. Without Jun-

117
00:07:41,370 --> 00:07:43,238
That's not my problem!

118
00:07:43,238 --> 00:07:47,108
If something happens to Jun, how will I explain it to his parents?

119
00:07:47,108 --> 00:07:50,137
So, you should leave. Go back to your own planet!

120
00:07:58,764 --> 00:08:00,274
Edo, how could you be such an idiot?!

121
00:08:00,274 --> 00:08:02,059
Huh? What's gotten into you?

122
00:08:02,059 --> 00:08:07,153
Planet Machina was blown up in an explosion! Blue Cop has no home to return to!

123
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:08,790
Huh... what?!

124
00:08:13,319 --> 00:08:16,473
If he had no home to go back to, he should have said that in the first place!

125
00:08:19,276 --> 00:08:21,831
That truck seems to be a little wobbly, isn't it?

126
00:08:21,831 --> 00:08:23,446
Coming through!

127
00:08:29,507 --> 00:08:30,774
Ugh...

128
00:08:43,971 --> 00:08:45,974
That was the wobbly truck!

129
00:08:45,974 --> 00:08:48,240
Oh man... was the driver dozing off?

130
00:08:52,956 --> 00:08:56,225
Oh no! We need to go alert the train, quick!

131
00:08:57,536 --> 00:08:59,994
Blue Cop... where are you?

132
00:09:04,322 --> 00:09:07,644
You wouldn't mind if I used the siren in this situation, would you?

133
00:09:07,644 --> 00:09:08,653
Blue Cop!

134
00:09:08,653 --> 00:09:10,913
Yes! Awaiting your command!

135
00:09:11,613 --> 00:09:14,149
We gotta push that truck out of the crossing!

136
00:09:14,149 --> 00:09:15,085
Yes!

137
00:09:17,099 --> 00:09:20,889
Hey, stop the train! Please stop! C'mon, stop!!

138
00:09:33,298 --> 00:09:35,988
This isn't working. I'm not strong enough on my own.

139
00:09:37,088 --> 00:09:38,029
Hey, Jun!

140
00:09:38,873 --> 00:09:40,215
Mega Trucker!

141
00:09:40,215 --> 00:09:42,245
Looks like an emergency. Need a hand?

142
00:09:43,045 --> 00:09:44,037
I could use one.

143
00:09:44,349 --> 00:09:45,932
Metal Breath, pickup!

144
00:09:47,826 --> 00:09:49,349
Mega Trucker, setup!

145
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,398
Scoot over. I'll help you with that!

146
00:10:05,625 --> 00:10:07,110
Just a little more!

147
00:10:11,365 --> 00:10:11,854
Now!

148
00:10:34,427 --> 00:10:39,774
So you spent thousands of years wandering the universe until you finally landed here on Earth?!

149
00:10:40,474 --> 00:10:43,899
Okay... from now on, planet Earth will be your new home.

150
00:10:43,899 --> 00:10:44,965
Really?

151
00:10:44,965 --> 00:10:48,548
I'm sure we will need your help in the future.

152
00:10:48,548 --> 00:10:50,939
Don't worry, I'll take good care of you guys!

153
00:10:50,939 --> 00:10:52,807
Planet Earth is...

154
00:10:52,807 --> 00:10:54,333
...our new home?

155
00:10:55,884 --> 00:10:58,072
Here, you can wipe your tears with this.

156
00:11:03,889 --> 00:11:05,879
Eugh...

